WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:03.374
Here is the updated Veri Gate walkthrough.

2
00:00:03.324 --> 00:00:09.768
We will follow a vehicle through the gate, then look at the inventory and user changes from your latest feedback.

3
00:00:10.613 --> 00:00:12.677
Start with the driver.

4
00:00:12.627 --> 00:00:19.044
Scan the badge or enter the employee number, confirm the record, and continue to the vehicle barcode.

5
00:00:19.863 --> 00:00:22.932
This barcode is not in inventory yet.

6
00:00:22.882 --> 00:00:26.013
The workflow accepts it and continues.

7
00:00:26.013 --> 00:00:31.104
When the movement is processed, the vehicle is added as ordinary inventory.

8
00:00:31.947 --> 00:00:36.459
Choose the direction, review the details, and submit the movement.

9
00:00:36.409 --> 00:00:41.847
After recording it, the scanner returns to the start, ready for the next driver.

10
00:00:42.697 --> 00:00:46.487
The same vehicle can leave through the usual driver checks.

11
00:00:46.437 --> 00:00:49.465
There is no inventory completion block.

12
00:00:49.465 --> 00:00:54.568
A barcode first encountered on exit is also added and logged in this version.

13
00:00:55.405 --> 00:01:00.948
In the console, Vehicles Added By Scan shows which records originated at the gate.

14
00:01:00.898 --> 00:01:04.545
Supervisors can fill in missing details later.

15
00:01:04.545 --> 00:01:08.320
Those details do not delay the vehicle's next movement.

16
00:01:09.155 --> 00:01:11.850
Users now have an Edit action.

17
00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:16.813
It opens their existing details, and saving updates that same user.

18
00:01:16.813 --> 00:01:20.962
Changes to the user's role are recorded in the audit history.

19
00:01:21.822 --> 00:01:24.968
The separate Manager role has been removed.

20
00:01:24.918 --> 00:01:33.152
The available roles are Scanner, Fleet Lead, Supervisor, and Admin. Existing Manager user records convert to Admin.

21
00:01:33.152 --> 00:01:38.255
These are still prototype accounts; secure login is part of the backend work.

22
00:01:39.113 --> 00:01:44.617
For a driver authorization override, the approver must be a Fleet Lead or above.

23
00:01:44.567 --> 00:01:47.299
A Scanner role cannot approve it.

24
00:01:47.299 --> 00:01:52.016
The driver checks remain in place alongside the new inventory behavior.

25
00:01:52.863 --> 00:01:56.666
Finally, the movement stays in the searchable history.

26
00:01:56.616 --> 00:02:00.173
The Android package includes these same revisions.

27
00:02:00.173 --> 00:02:06.114
This remains a device-local review build, with shared data and synchronization still ahead.
